From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] library: ChaCha20 at -O2 in a build for size

Fathom builds mbedTLS with -Os (external.mk). There GCC doesn't inline
chacha20_quarter_round, and ChaCha20-Poly1305 runs at half the speed
(measured: 251 against 561 MB/s on a computer); AES-GCM is as fast or faster.
ChaCha20 alone at -O2 brings it back for a few hundred bytes. Its options come
after CMAKE_C_FLAGS on the command line, so its -O2 wins.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Fathom's build choice]

--- a/library/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/library/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -127,6 +127,10 @@
     ssl_tls13_client.c
     ssl_tls13_generic.c
 )
+
+# ChaCha20 at -O2 in a build for size: at -Os its quarter round isn't inlined,
+# and ChaCha20-Poly1305 runs at half the speed
+set_source_files_properties(chacha20.c PROPERTIES COMPILE_OPTIONS -O2)

 if(GEN_FILES)
     find_package(Perl REQUIRED)
